module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.witnesses_red_on_main_with_no_failure_mode_row

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungRead, FoundOnRung, BelowCeiling }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data witnesses_red_on_main_with_no_failure_mode_row: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "witnesses_red_on_main_with_no_failure_mode_row" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "an instrument label whose run executes the witness population and states, per identity, whether it is green at the default branch head and whether the required path runs it",
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "**a witness red at origin/main has no row, so every PR that touches its module rediscovers and re-attributes it** (INVALID STATE: a committed witness fails under `gunbc run --claim-run` at the default branch head and nothing records that, which test, or whether the required path runs it).",

    "HARM: each lane has to re-measure the failure against main to show it is not its own, and a lane that skips the comparison either blames itself or absorbs the red. SPECIMEN (gunbc#14384, main 6ae9b3b9591, executed with `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry <witness> --claim-run`): test.claim.rung_drop_superseded_standing_witness the_live_roster_loss_holders_resolve_and_stand; test.claim.compiler_frontend_program_status_witness every_declared_instrument_is_distinct_and_awaited; test.claim.exact_witness_admission_witness no_batch_mixes_a_pre_verdict_row_with_an_assertion_false_row and both_red_expectations_are_known_red_but_only_one_expects_a_pre_verdict_refusal. Whether any of the four is on the required path was not established by that lane.",

    "SPECIMEN, MECHANISM (D13, main 1acf79a8af4c, remote `claim_batch --claim-run` of v2.test.claim.compiler.dependency_demand_census with a probe printing `demand_census_row_line` per row): 14 of 22 claims FAIL on main, among them demand_through_a_transparent_callee_is_equal_holds, and the eight that pass are partly vacuous (their expected verdict is unobserved). THE REDUCER NEVER RAN, and a chain of unjustified links hid it, each behind the one before. LINK 1, STALE FIXTURE, FIXED: ddc_ingest omitted std.types while every fixture source imports `std.types { Bool }`, so 13 of 15 rows read unobserved resolve_module_not_found; the real std.types imports std.algebra, a world the fixture cannot supply, so the ingest carries a stub declaring `type Bool = True | False` exactly as dag/std/types.dag does. LINK 2, CENSUS DEFECT, FIXED: demand_census_authored_reading resolved a TYPE expression under the module-root value-category context, so since #14090 every `uses net: Network` was reference_category_mismatch, collapsed with three other arms into AuthoredTypeUnresolved; it now resolves under resolve_ctx_with_reference_category(TypeOccurrence) (v2.compiler.resolve unchanged; no other type-expression resolve_node site exists). LINK 3, CENSUS DEFECT, FIXED: since #14209 every list introduction heads with a generated reference to std.algebra.FreeMonoid and demand_fact_node counted it as a callee (callee_outside_closure at FreeMonoid); a list introduction is not a call, recognised by v2.std.list_introduction list_introduction_elements_optional, the reader eval uses. LINK 4, RESOLVED (one resolve defect, neither the fixture nor the walk): every module with `import std.resources { Network }` and `requires Network` was REFUSED AT RESOLVE with resolve_reason_reference_category_mismatch at the requires member, so no OperationFact existed (census: function_not_declared, callee_outside_closure, empty vocabulary). Cause, v2.compiler.resolve: the arrow's resource-requirements slot walked its members in the ambient VALUE category although every member names a resource, which v2.std.symbol_index classifies TypeOccurrence; it now walks resolve_ctx_type_role. Ablated by remote claim_batch: reverting that one edit returns the same nine census claims to FAIL. FALSIFIED HYPOTHESIS, do not re-apply: an earlier diagnosis named v2.std.symbol_index symbol_index_candidate_category (marks written at the declaring path but read at the binding path) as the earliest unjustified link; the edit that read marks at the declaring path was ablated and FALSIFIED for this population: with it reverted all 21 census claims still pass and an eligibility claim at that grain passes, because an imported resource is already a TypeOccurrence through its declaration node shape. The real cause is the value-role walk above. REAL CORPUS, REPAIR UNMEASURED: a remote census over the 68 files whose requires names an imported declaration (selected by identity) plus their 2069-file import closure refused the identical 3249 modules at the merge base and at the repair head, so no accepted-to-refused flip exists within that population and the repair is not observable there. The specimen gunbc.auth.approval_ntfy_publish (service ntfy.Publish, operation PublishMessage, requires Network imported from std.resources) is refused in both arms; its own refusal causes were not obtained, since gunbc run --function reports pool_modules=refused without a cause and is the seed route. Sibling rows show importee_refused via extdeps/shell/exec.dag (service_realization_argv_refused). TRIGGER: the specimen repair becomes observable when its own refusal causes clear. An earlier count of 68 files was a grep, not a measurement. REASON COLLAPSE, STILL OPEN (a resolve_module_not_found refusal also carries an EMPTY unbound_locus): the four AuthoredTypeUnresolved arms (shell absent, lowering absent, resolve rejected, no declaration path) still print one cause; carrying resolve's reason in the row hit a closure-diagnostics cascade in which the record DemandCensusRow was erased to T (no field 'standings' on type 'T'), not yet reduced. AFTER LINKS 1-4 (remote claim_batch at the repair head): all 21 claims of v2.test.claim.compiler.dependency_demand_census PASS (the 22nd line counted earlier was the removed probe), every one of the nine link-4 fails now green; the 10 reducer claims of v2.test.claim.compiler.dependency_demand PASS (they were not exercised before); neighbours v2.test.claim.normalize.operation_requires_edge (15) and v2.test.claim.name_resolve.kind_aware_binding (21) PASS. Classification at claim identity: link 1 stale fixture, links 2-4 genuine defects in census and resolve, never environment-blocked. ",

    "SPECIMEN, WHOLE-FILE REFUSAL (2026-10-24, main 16d6f1c5636, executed with `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --entry src/v2/test/claim/activation_dependency.dag --claim-run` on one remote dispatch): v2.test.claim.activation_dependency did not resolve at all -- undefined variable `d` and fields `d` / `eclaration` not found in type `Edge` -- so NONE of its claims ran: 0 PASS, 0 FAIL, rc=1. Cause: three Edge literals (acd_positional, acd_pattern_edge, acd_body_edge) were spliced by the Edge.declaration edit of gunbc#14662 (a stray `d,` plus a duplicated declaration field split across two lines). A refused claim module reports no FAIL line, so a lane that greps FAIL reads it as green. After repairing the three literals: 15 PASS, 0 FAIL, rc=0. Found by cool-crane-86 while consuming v2.compiler.activation_dependency for the effect-pair census.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT 1, mitigatable: the red is visible to whoever runs the witness and to no gate. CEILING 3, structurally guaranteed for the enrolled population: a witness on the required path cannot be red at main because the merge queue refuses it; the unenrolled remainder is a ratchet.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: an instrument label whose run executes the witness population and states, per identity, whether it is green at the default branch head and whether the required path runs it. SUFFICIENT FOR: the four specimens above being counted, or shown absent, by that run rather than by this row.",

    "SPECIMEN (merry-raven-863, gunbc#15104; base C-host dad136e4d8b4, and C-host 59170506f4fe before it): test.claim.fabric.fabric_control_plane_witness w_the_broker_refuses_a_winner_admitted_for_another_demand and w_the_broker_refuses_a_winner_admitted_for_another_work. Both expect the broker to refuse a permit naming another demand (or another work) -- PermitNamesAnotherUseForCell, the arm gunbc#10802 added -- and both read NoCellAdmissible instead. Selection refuses the only candidate before the permit is read: considered = [OfferNotFungible { fungibility: ShapeAxesNotCovered { unmet: [MemoryNotOffered { required: Measure { count: 22571538728 } }] }, offer: offer-1 }]. The fixture demand (gunbc.floor.floor_demand floor_demand) now requires memory, and the fixture offer (cp_offer_sized, unstated_envelope()) offers none. So both claims stopped exercising the permit arm they name, and the arm has no executing witness on that route. BISECT, each point running the claim alone with `gunbc run --claim-run --function <claim>` on a seed built at that sha: PASS at 903e6c15e586 (2026-09-09, gunbc#10802); FAIL at d41c94e3c232 and 132c780e4a6d (2026-09-21); FAIL at every later point tried (68ad0673deb7, 947458435a02, 28415165a129, 1f6b4107a046, 4a5d25ed769b). The two points between, 66d683bc8655 and b90b6cf147a2 (gunbc#11672, 2026-09-20, the change that derives the floor's microVM shape from typed floor-demand receipts and the only change in the window touching the memory axis), do not resolve the witness, so the introducing change is bounded by that window, not executed. The fix belongs to whoever owns the fixture's offer shape (an offer covering the demand's memory axis, so the claim reaches the permit arm again), and is not taken in gunbc#15104.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: a red you did not cause is a fact about main, not about your lane. Run the same witness at origin/main, cite the sha, and check this ledger before attributing it.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
